cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mcp-vlei: verifiable organizational identity for the Model Context Protocol"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chu
    given-names: Ting-Yi
repository-code: "https://github.com/zuemen/mcp-vlei"
abstract: >-
  An additive extension to the Model Context Protocol that carries GLEIF vLEI
  credentials, so a tool call can establish which legal entity is accountable and
  under what delegated authority. Every layer MCP authenticates proves control of
  a domain or the identity of a human user; none expresses a legal entity. The
  extension travels in the fields MCP already reserves for extensions and does not
  modify the core schema.
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - vLEI
  - GLEIF
  - KERI
  - ACDC
  - agent identity
  - organizational identity
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.2"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
